{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKpvtn4Zm1mPaLmjgaPZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #174 with status **done**: the engineer triage role (`triage:engineer`) will write the plan, and the engineer worker will implement it. The routing file is `.ard/174/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Why it's ready to route:** this is a clear bug fix. Cleanup of a job's home folder fails because Go's module cache is read-only, so those folders are never deleted. The fix belongs in the local executor's step cleanup (`internal/executor/local/proc_unix.go` and `local.go`) and in the Reaper's retention cleanup. The required tests are a read-only folder holding a read-only file, and a symlink that points outside the job home and must not be followed.\n- **Why only the engineer:** the only triage roles that exist are engineer and lead. No architect or product-manager role exists to route to. The `eng-review` reviewer runs on every pull request because the config gives it no `when:` rule, so it needs no extra entry.\n- **Open issue for a maintainer:** with no architect, the engineer's plan has to decide the optional shared Go module cache (`GOMODCACHE` or `GOFLAGS`) on its own. That includes the risk that one job could tamper with a cache other jobs share, and how the cache is mounted into Docker jobs. A maintainer may want to review that choice, or keep this issue to the cleanup fix and track the shared cache in a separate issue."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":451,"cache_read_input_tokens":13048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":451},"output_tokens":460,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"caf8e6d9-bc98-44df-8de7-fba69